  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Mammoth is undergoing a sharp operational inflection driven by a strategic pivot toward higher-return segments, particularly its aviation and equipment rental businesses. The company has streamlined its portfolio through divestitures, exiting lower-margin activities while demand fundamentals in remaining verticals have strengthened. This repositioning has shifted the mix toward more capital-light, recurring revenue streams, and management now describes a clear, improving trajectory after a long period of uncertainty.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership executed a deliberate portfolio simplification, shedding non-core assets and aggressively removing costs from the structure, which restored positive profitability and prompted an upward guidance revision. The CFO highlighted that the repositioning is now showing in results, acknowledging lingering segment-level execution issues but emphasizing a broader return to financial health. A large, subsequent insider purchase by a long-standing institutional holder reinforces the market’s perception of management credibility and conviction in the ongoing turnaround.",
